[93.195845, "o", "Lab doctor: Linux x86_64, Python 3.12.3 running this check\r\n\r\n  ✓  Python 3.11+ in the shared .venv         Python 3.12.3\r\n  ✓  git installed                            /usr/bin/git\r\n  ✓  make installed                           /usr/bin/make\r\n  ✓  Docker installed                         /usr/bin/docker\r\n  !  Docker engine running                    the engine runs, but your user may not use it\r\n        next step: Use `sudo docker ...`, or add yourself to the docker group (root-level access, see docs/SETUP.md): sudo usermod -aG docker $USER, then log out and back in.\r\n  -  Docker can run a container\r\n  ✓  Ollama running (API on 127.0.0.1:11434)  Ollama 0.40.11\r\n  ✓  Ollama listens on 127.0.0.1 only         listening on 127.0.0.1\r\n  ✓  Lab models downloaded                    gemma3:1b, embeddinggemma\r\n  ✓  Memory (RAM)                             15.6 GB\r\n  ✓  Free disk space                          81.9 GB free\r\n\r\nReady, with 1 warning(s) above. You can start the labs.\r\n"]
[93.207239, "o", "\r\nNext: activate the shared environment in each new terminal, then start Lab M1:\r\n  source .venv/bin/activate\r\n  cd labs/m01 && cat README.md\r\nLabs M4, M6, M8 and M9 install their own packages with \"make setup\" inside their folder.\r\n"]
